config BR2_PACKAGE_X11LIBRE_XSERVER
	bool "X11Libre Xfbdev server"
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU
	select BR2_PACKAGE_XORGPROTO
	select BR2_PACKAGE_XLIB_LIBXFONT2
	select BR2_PACKAGE_XLIB_XTRANS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PIXMAN
	help
	  Xfbdev, the kdrive framebuffer X server, from the X11Libre fork of
	  xorg-server.

	  Upstream xorg-server dropped the small kdrive servers - 21.1.23 ships
	  only Xephyr, which needs a host X server. X11Libre restores Xfbdev on
	  a modern, actively maintained codebase, which matters here because the
	  full Xorg server plus its modules measures 3.0 MB against a flash
	  budget of roughly 7.4 MB shared with everything else.

	  Draws into /dev/fb0. On this board that is the DRM driver's fbdev
	  emulation, so writes still reach the plane update path and keep PPA
	  scaling and the reduced render size.

	  https://github.com/X11Libre/xserver
